A||||2||Adrift||redo Brake system - where to get parts in Canada?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-22-2001||08:45 AM||||I want to rebuild the break system on my car (replace rubber lines with stainless steel, new/rebuilt calipers & rotors all around, new emerg. break cables and what not, etc.) but don't know where to go to get all these parts. I know I can go to Canadian tire or NAPA to get the stainless steel lines, and a Pontiac dealership should be able to order me the the emerg break parts, but what about the calipers and rotors? Where do I take them to get rebuilt/replaced? (Which ones do you rebuild which ones do you replace?<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||11-22-2001||08:58 AM||||Usually any parts store will sell you rebuilt calipers and it's cheaper if you give them your old ones as a core.  For the price of having rotors machined, you should just buy new ones.  I go to McMaster Autoparts at Warden and Eglinton (Across from Wal-Mart).  But Race-Tech (Fiero Shop) has everything in stock, and you know you will get the right stuff.  416-747-5728<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||11-22-2001||05:51 PM||||If you are redoing your entire brakes It would be a good time to upgrade! If you have a pre88 fiero maybe search the Technical area for the Beretta upgrade info. If you have an 88 fiero upgrading probably isn't worth it.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com</A>  had cross drilled rotors and such also. Might be worth checking out.||||reg||14
